WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.455 --> 00:00:15.937
the rest of the day we were busy making our preparations.

2
00:00:16.778 --> 00:00:20.361
We scrubbed the decks of our sailboat and polished its two brass cannons.

3
00:00:21.282 --> 00:00:23.584
My wife made sure we had the proper clothes to wear.

4
00:00:24.424 --> 00:00:27.027
The next morning we set sail with the kayak in tow.

5
00:00:27.807 --> 00:00:29.268
We pulled close to the English ship.

6
00:00:30.249 --> 00:00:33.252
After dropping anchor, Fritz and I then paddled toward it.

7
00:00:34.016 --> 00:00:36.157
The captain and crew were astonished to see us.

8
00:00:36.177 --> 00:00:38.597
"Welcome aboard!"

9
00:00:38.877 --> 00:00:39.638
cried the captain.

10
00:00:40.438 --> 00:00:44.839
He introduced himself as Captain Littlestone and asked us to follow him to his cabin.

11
00:00:44.859 --> 00:00:48.540
"How did you come to live here, so far from Europe?"

12
00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:49.380
he asked.

13
00:00:50.281 --> 00:00:53.922
I told him the story of our shipwreck and the tale of Miss Montrose.

14
00:00:54.922 --> 00:00:58.323
At the mention of Jenny's name, he stood up and clasped my hand.

15
00:00:59.183 --> 00:01:01.704
"Let me thank you on behalf of Colonel Montrose.

16
00:01:02.524 --> 00:01:04.265
I came to these shores in search of her."

17
00:01:04.285 --> 00:01:06.466
"But how did you know where to look?"

18
00:01:06.927 --> 00:01:07.507
asked Fritz.

19
00:01:08.468 --> 00:01:12.710
"Her father never gave up hope of finding her," replied Captain Littlestone.

20
00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:17.953
"A few weeks ago in Sydney, Australia, I met some survivors from her ship.

21
00:01:18.733 --> 00:01:20.554
They told me where the storm had hit.

22
00:01:21.315 --> 00:01:25.557
I decided to search for Miss Montrose on my way to the Cape of Good Hope in Africa."

23
00:01:26.298 --> 00:01:30.080
Then Captain Littlestone begged to be introduced to Jenny and the rest of our family.

24
00:01:30.752 --> 00:01:33.174
He sent an officer to fetch them from our sailboat.

25
00:01:35.996 --> 00:01:37.818
We had a very pleasant lunch aboard the ship.

26
00:01:37.838 --> 00:01:39.639
"An invalid, Mr.

27
00:01:39.679 --> 00:01:42.782
Wolston, is sailing with us to the Cape," said the captain.

28
00:01:43.542 --> 00:01:46.545
Mr. Wolston's wife and two daughters were also on board.

29
00:01:46.565 --> 00:01:51.048
"It was thought that the sea air would improve his health," said the captain.

30
00:01:51.068 --> 00:01:55.472
"But this week's storm was not good for him, and he has been resting onshore."

31
00:01:56.353 --> 00:02:00.256
We were eager to meet the Wolston family, so we paid them a visit that afternoon.

32
00:02:01.012 --> 00:02:03.034
Tents had been pitched in the shade of some trees.

33
00:02:03.874 --> 00:02:07.757
Mr. Wolston was seated by one of them, enjoying the cool sea breeze.

34
00:02:08.718 --> 00:02:11.800
"I'm delighted to meet you," he said as he introduced his family.

35
00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:14.762
We had not met so many people for years.

36
00:02:15.582 --> 00:02:16.643
We talked and talked.

37
00:02:17.624 --> 00:02:19.605
Before we knew it, darkness was falling.

38
00:02:20.286 --> 00:02:23.428
The captain kindly provided tents so that we could stay the night.

39
00:02:24.228 --> 00:02:29.072
The boys and Miss Montrose slept in the tents while my wife and I retreated to our sailboat.

40
00:02:29.824 --> 00:02:32.645
That night we had a long conversation about returning to Europe.

41
00:02:33.485 --> 00:02:35.986
At first I did not know how my wife felt about this.

42
00:02:36.766 --> 00:02:39.687
But finally I said that I considered New Switzerland our home.

43
00:02:39.707 --> 00:02:45.689
"I want to stay here too," she said, "as long as you and at least two of our

44
00:02:45.729 --> 00:02:47.389
sons also wish to remain.

45
00:02:48.089 --> 00:02:51.711
Two boys may return to Europe if they send back colonists to join us."

46
00:02:52.511 --> 00:02:53.851
But which of our sons would go?

47
00:02:54.591 --> 00:02:56.212
We decided to leave that up to them.

48
00:02:57.676 --> 00:03:01.600
The next morning we suggested that Captain Littlestone should bring his ship to Safety Bay.

49
00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:05.903
That way his crew and the Wolston family could visit us at Rockburg.

50
00:03:06.684 --> 00:03:10.267
When they arrived onshore, our visitors were amazed at our house.

51
00:03:11.148 --> 00:03:14.931
The young people spent the afternoon roaming about our formerly quiet grounds.

52
00:03:15.812 --> 00:03:17.053
Mr. Wolston took a nap.

53
00:03:17.914 --> 00:03:19.415
He was able to join us for supper.

54
00:03:19.435 --> 00:03:24.540
"The hope of residing among you gives me new life," he said with a smile.

55
00:03:25.352 --> 00:03:29.716
"If it is agreeable to you, I would like to remain here with my wife and my older

56
00:03:29.756 --> 00:03:32.459
daughter. Her health is also delicate.

57
00:03:33.239 --> 00:03:36.943
My younger daughter would go temporarily to her brother at the Cape of Good Hope."

58
00:03:36.963 --> 00:03:39.705
"You are welcome to stay here with us," I said.

59
00:03:39.725 --> 00:03:42.848
"Hurrah for New Switzerland!"

60
00:03:43.288 --> 00:03:44.049
shouted everyone.

61
00:03:44.069 --> 00:03:47.332
"Won't someone cheer for those of us who are leaving?"

62
00:03:47.752 --> 00:03:48.333
asked Jenny.

63
00:03:48.353 --> 00:03:50.395
"Three cheers for England!"

64
00:03:50.715 --> 00:03:51.296
cried Fritz.

65
00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:55.622
"And success and happiness to those of us who return to Europe!"

66
00:03:56.442 --> 00:03:59.984
When it was silent again, I said, "Fritz and Jenny seem to be leaving us.

67
00:04:00.885 --> 00:04:02.085
Who else is going to Europe?"

68
00:04:02.926 --> 00:04:06.228
"I want to go back to get a good education," said Franz.

69
00:04:07.108 --> 00:04:09.710
But Ernest and Jack announced that they would be staying with us.

70
00:04:10.710 --> 00:04:13.892
Later that night Fritz told me that he intended to marry Jenny.

71
00:04:14.773 --> 00:04:18.935
My wife and I approved of the match although we would miss them—and Franz—so much.

72
00:04:19.795 --> 00:04:22.989
Having found Jenny, Captain Littlestone was eager to depart.

73
00:04:23.789 --> 00:04:25.950
It is now the night before the ship leaves.

74
00:04:26.871 --> 00:04:28.932
I'm writing in my journal for the last time.

75
00:04:29.632 --> 00:04:32.854
Tomorrow I will present this journal to Fritz to take back to Europe.

76
00:04:33.734 --> 00:04:35.235
From afar I greet you, Europe.

77
00:04:36.015 --> 00:04:37.996
I greet you, dear old Switzerland.

78
00:04:38.877 --> 00:04:45.180
Like you, may New Switzerland flourish and prosper—good, happy, and free!
